      children: "Q131. Laid vs Lay vs Lied? Answer: He lay on the bed (past of lie)\nQ132. Antonym of Transient? Answer: Permanent\nQ133. Synonym of Perilous? Answer: Dangerous\nQ134. One word: Speech without preparation? Answer: Extempore\nQ135. Hit the nail on the head? Answer: Describe exactly\nQ136. Passive: Children are playing cricket. Answer: Cricket is being played\nQ137. Neither teacher nor students (is/are)? Answer: are\nQ138. Misspelled? a) Maintenance b) Occurrence c) Embarrass d) Privelege. Answer: Privelege\nQ139. Ameliorate antonym? Answer: Worsen\nQ140. Committee (has/have) decided? Answer: has"
